---
// The privacy policy California's Online Privacy Protection Act (CalOPPA) requires of any site
// that collects personal information, written to match what this site and the team tools
// actually do. Change it when that changes: a new analytics or ad tool, a new provider, or
// texting campaigns. The cookie table must list everything Consent.astro and the pages store.
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';

const email = 'beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy Policy"
  kicker="Legal"
  updated="October 23, 2026"
  description="What FutureClarity Technologies collects when you visit or ask for a free quote, the cookies we use and only with your OK, who helps us run things, and your choices."
>
  <p>
    FutureClarity Technologies ("we", "us") builds and looks after websites and apps, and sets up
    automations, for businesses. This policy explains what we collect through futureclaritytechnologies.com and in
    our work, how we use it, and the choices you have. Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
    or call <a href="tel:+18185850475">(818) 585-0475</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="summary">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We collect what you send us to ask for a quote, and use it to help you.</li>
      <li>We count visits without cookies. Google Analytics and Google Ads load only if you say yes.</li>
      <li>We don't sell your information or use it to show you ads on other sites.</li>
      <li>We never share your phone number or texting consent with anyone for their marketing.</li>
      <li>You can change your cookie choices, or ask us to delete your information, any time.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>When you ask for a free quote:</strong> your name, your business's name, the phone number or
      email you choose to give us, the services you pick, any note you add, and which ad or website
      brought you to us, if any.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>When you call, text or email us:</strong> your contact details and what you send.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>When you visit the site:</strong> our host, Cloudflare, processes standard technical
      details, such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you request, to deliver the site and
      protect it from abuse. Cloudflare Web Analytics also gives us visit counts (pages viewed, the site
      you came from, device and browser type, and country) without cookies and without identifying you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Only if you allow it:</strong> Google Analytics and Google Ads cookies. See
      <a href="#cookies">Cookies and similar tools</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>About businesses we might work with:</strong> we use publicly available business
      information, such as business listings, public websites and Google reviews, to find local
      businesses that could use our services. We keep business contact details and notes about our
      outreach.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and similar tools</h2>
  <p>
    The first time you visit, we ask before anything from Google loads. "Accept all", "Reject all" and
    "Choose" are equally easy, and nothing is turned on until you pick. Change your mind any time with
    <button type="button" class="linkish" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</button>, also in the
    footer of every page.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Cookies and browser storage we use">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Set by</th><th scope="col">Why</th><th scope="col">How long</th><th scope="col">Needs your OK?</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>fc-consent</code> (browser storage)</td><td>Us</td><td>Remembers your cookie choices</td><td>12 months</td><td>No, needed to respect them</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>fc-src</code> (browser storage)</td><td>Us</td><td>Which ad or website brought you, sent along with your quote request so we know which ads work. It stays on this site.</td><td>30 days</td><td>No</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>fc-booked</code> (browser storage, this tab only)</td><td>Us</td><td>Stops the form asking twice after you send it</td><td>Until you close the tab</td><td>No, needed</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_…</code> cookies</td><td>Google Analytics</td><td>Counts visits and how pages are used, so we can improve the site</td><td>About 13 months</td><td>Yes: "Analytics"</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>_gcl_au</code> and other Google Ads cookies</td><td>Google Ads</td><td>Tells us which ad led to a quote request</td><td>Up to 90 days</td><td>Yes: "Advertising"</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    If you allow analytics, we record things like which pages you view, which buttons you tap (such as
    "Get a free quote" or our phone number), and when a quote request is sent. We never send your name,
    phone number, email or notes to Google. If you allow advertising, Google Ads learns that a visit from
    one of our ads led to a quote request. We turn off ad personalization, so we don't use it to show you
    ads elsewhere. Google handles this data under its
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>,
    and you can also block Google Analytics everywhere with Google's
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">opt-out add-on</a>.
  </p>
  <p>Our team's own tools, such as our dashboard, also use browser storage to keep team members signed in.</p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to you, set up your free consultation, prepare your quote, and provide the work you hire us for.</li>
    <li>To understand which pages and ads bring people to us, and improve the site.</li>
    <li>To contact businesses about our services, by phone, in person, or by email with an easy way to opt out.</li>
    <li>To keep the site and our records secure, and to meet our legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Calls and texts</h2>
  <p>
    If you give us your phone number when you book or contact us, we may call or text you about your
    request, sometimes using automated tools. We don't send marketing texts without your permission. How
    often we text depends on your request. Reply STOP to any text from us and we'll stop texting you, or
    HELP for help. Message and data rates may apply. See our <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> for more about
    texts.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We don't share mobile numbers or text-message consent with anyone for their marketing.</strong>
    Your text-message opt-in and consent are never shared with or sold to third parties. The providers
    that carry our messages handle them only to deliver them.
  </p>

  <h2>Who helps us run things</h2>
  <p>
    We don't sell personal information. We use a few service providers, who handle information only to
    provide their service to us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the website, protects it from abuse, and gives us cookie-free visit counts.</li>
    <li><strong>Supabase</strong> stores quote requests and our client and outreach records.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong>, only if you allow it, runs Google Analytics and Google Ads. The website's fonts are served from our own site, so loading a page sends nothing to Google.</li>
    <li>Our <strong>email and phone providers</strong> carry the messages we send and receive.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information when the law requires it, to protect our rights or someone's
    safety, or to a new owner if our business is sold or merged, who would be bound by this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>When we build for a client</h2>
  <p>
    The websites, apps and automations we build and run for clients can handle their customers'
    information, such as names and phone numbers for booking reminders. We handle it only to provide the services, following the client's
    instructions. The client's own privacy policy covers how they use it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Change or withdraw your cookie choices any time with <button type="button" class="linkish" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</button>.</li>
    <li>
      Ask to know what personal information we hold about you, to get a copy, to correct it or to delete
      it, or tell us to stop contacting you. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> or call
      <a href="tel:+18185850475">(818) 585-0475</a>. We'll confirm the request comes from you, usually by
      replying to the email or phone number we have on file, and respond within 45 days. Someone you
      authorize can make a request for you.
    </li>
    <li>Every sales email from us includes a way to opt out, and we honor it.</li>
    <li>We won't treat you differently for making any of these requests.</li>
    <li>
      California residents: we don't sell personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral
      advertising, and we don't share it with other companies for their own marketing (California Civil
      Code § 1798.83).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>
    If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, we keep advertising cookies off
    automatically, and the cookie choices show that. We treat the signal as a request to opt out of any
    sale or sharing of your information. You can still choose whether to allow analytics.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep quote requests, client records and outreach notes as long as we need them for the work, our
    records and our legal obligations, then delete them. Google Analytics keeps visit data for no more
    than 14 months. Cookie-free visit counts are kept only as totals. You can ask us to delete your
    information sooner.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses HTTPS, the database that holds quote requests is locked so only our team can read it,
    and access is limited to the people who need it. No system is perfectly secure, but we take
    reasonable steps to protect what you share with us.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our site and services are for businesses. They aren't directed to children, and we don't knowingly
    collect information from anyone under 16.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When we change this policy, we'll post the new version here with a new date. If a change affects how
    we use information you've already given us, we'll ask first.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    FutureClarity Technologies, San Fernando Valley, California ·
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> · <a href="tel:+18185850475">(818) 585-0475</a>
  </p>
</Doc>
